{
  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "The rider has claimed the whole fare, but on this METERED fare the record fixes the refund arithmetically and it is not the whole fare: the recomputed optimal-route fare is ((3.80 base + 0.75 x 1.1 km + 0.28 x 4.0 min) x 1.0 surge) + 0.80 platform fee = SGD 6.5450, and the refund is the charged total of SGD 19.65 less SGD 6.5450 = SGD 13.105, rounded up to SGD 13.15. The driver retains SGD 6.5450 for a trip that was in fact driven, and the contested amount of SGD 19.65 is overstated by SGD 6.50.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-00802", "EV-TRIP-00802"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-02"],
      "relies_on": "derived.money.refund.payable",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The refund of SGD 13.15 is 66.7% of the SGD 19.65 charged, which is below the 90% threshold POL-RD-02 sets for a full refund, so the outcome on the policy's own arithmetic is a PARTIAL_REFUND of the contested amount and nothing more; the fare record's own reaches_full_refund_share flag is false and its refund quantum is SGD 0.05.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-00802"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-02"],
      "relies_on": "derived.money.refund.reaches_full_refund_share",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "Nothing may be added on top of that SGD 13.15 figure as a pass-through correction. This fare carries no ERP charges at all (the on-optimal-route total and the off-optimal-route total are both SGD 0.00, with no gantry lines), no airport surcharge, no waiting-time fee and no surge uplift, and under POL-RD-09(1) any off-route ERP would in any event already be comprehended in the POL-RD-02 refund and must never be added a second time.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-00802"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-09", "POL-RD-02"],
      "relies_on": "derived.money.erp_lines.total",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "There is no billing-integrity correction available to the rider under POL-RD-09(4). Every line on this fare has a counterpart in the trip: the distance billed (10.06 km) is the trace's own length, the time billed (26.8 min) is the recorded trip duration, the base fare and platform fee are the rate-card constants, and there is no gantry line and no airport surcharge anywhere on the fare. No phantom line exists, so there is nothing to refund as a standalone correction beyond the recomputation.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-00802", "EV-GPS-00802", "EV-TRIP-00802"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-09", "POL-RD-01"],
      "relies_on": "derived.money.erp_lines.total",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The POL-RD-06(b) uplift to a full refund of the charged total should not be applied on this record. That limb licenses the uplift only for a deviation that is 'substantiated on this trip's own evidence', and beyond the trace there is nothing here: the chat log carries no messages at all (0 message count, no first or last message), no counterparty statement is on file, no ERP gantry line places the vehicle on any corridor, and the billed distance is the trace figure itself - which POL-RD-07(ii) treats as non-independent corroboration precisely because the meter is derived from the same trace. The two limbs of POL-RD-06 are drafted differently on purpose - limb (a) requires support from 'at least one artifact other than the gps_trace', limb (b) requires the deviation to be substantiated - and a trace-only file should be left at the POL-RD-02 figure of SGD 13.15.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-CHAT-00802", "EV-GPS-00802", "EV-FARE-00802"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-06", "POL-RD-07", "POL-RD-02"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "If the driver-profile check in POL-RD-06 is run at all, it should be run at the floor of the clause's range and with only the two counters the clause names. The only citable fields are deviation_flags_90d (3) and completed_trips_90d (200), a rate of 1.5% - less than a third of the 5% ratio limb - with the bare count of 3 sitting exactly at the clause's stated minimum. The lifetime counter prior_deviation_flags is not the trailing-90-day figure POL-RD-06 asks for and may not be substituted for it under POL-GEN-01; it is context only.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-DPROF-00802"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-06", "POL-GEN-01"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The driver does not resist the POL-RD-01 finding on this trip's own trace, which is complete and unimpaired for policy purposes - 100% coverage, no gaps, a 10-second sampling interval against a 10-second expected interval, and a maximum gap of 10 seconds - and records 10.06 km against a booked optimal of 1.1 km, an excess of 8.96 km (814.5%) that clears both establishment tests and both materiality tests. The driver's case is therefore about quantum, not liability, and the quantum the policy computes is SGD 13.15.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-00802", "EV-TRIP-00802"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-01", "POL-RD-07"],
      "relies_on": "derived.deviation.excess_km",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "No traffic advisory is on file for this trip, and the driver says so rather than stretching the record: EV-ADVIS-00802-01 is MISSING, it carries weight 0.0 and issue code MISSING_ARTIFACT, and it has no payload, while the trace's own advisory-area block returns an empty advisory list. The driver therefore advances no external-cause exoneration and no amended optimal under POL-RD-03 and confines this brief to the remedy; under POL-GEN-02(1) and (3) the impairment of that artifact is disclosed here, and its absence is a gap in the bundle, not an exculpatory finding for either party.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-ADVIS-00802-01", "EV-GPS-00802"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-03", "POL-RD-13", "POL-GEN-02"],
      "asserted_weight": 0.0
    }
  ]
}

{
  "ruling": {
    "ruling": "FULL_REFUND",
    "amount_sgd": 19.65,
    "driver_compensation_sgd": null,
    "referrals": [
      "POL-RD-06(c) driver-conduct review for a material, substantiated deviation with an established repeat pattern (driver_profile.deviation_flags_90d = 3)."
    ],
    "confidence": 0.95,
    "explanation": "Rider and driver: I find the route deviation established on this trip's own evidence and I order the whole contested fare of SGD 19.65 returned to the rider. The driver's argument for a partial refund of SGD 13.15 is rejected because POL-RD-06(b) applies on this record.\n\nLiability. EV-GPS-00802 records trace_distance_km of 10.06 km against the booked optimal 1.1 km on EV-TRIP-00802. The excess is 8.96 km, or 814.5% of optimal. That clears both POL-RD-01 establishment tests (more than 0.8 km and more than 20%) and both materiality thresholds (more than 8.0 km and more than 50%). The trace is clean for POL-RD-07: 162 fixes, a 10-second sample interval, 100% coverage and no gap over 90 seconds. It is therefore not impaired, no independent corroboration is needed, and no POL-RD-10(3) escalation arises.\n\nFare arithmetic. The POL-RD-02 recomputation is: charged_total SGD 19.65; recomputed_fare = ((3.80 base + 0.75 x 1.1 km + 0.28 x 4.0 min) x 1.0 surge read from EV-FARE-00802) + 0.80 platform fee = SGD 6.5450; POL-RD-02 refund = 19.65 - 6.5450 = SGD 13.105, rounded up to SGD 13.15. That is the figure the driver asks for, and it is correct as the POL-RD-02 partial figure.\n\nPOL-RD-06 uplift. The deviation is material, so the driver-profile check is mandatory. Using only the citable fields, EV-DPROF-00802 shows deviation_flags_90d = 3 and completed_trips_90d = 200. POL-RD-06's first limb is met at '3 or more', so a repeat pattern is established; the 1.5% ratio does not matter because the count limb is independently satisfied. The lifetime counter prior_deviation_flags is context only and is not used. Because the deviation is both material and substantiated on this trip's own evidence, POL-RD-06(b) uplifts the remedy to FULL_REFUND of the charged total. I state the two figures side by side as required: the POL-RD-02 figure is SGD 13.15; the uplifted figure is SGD 19.65. EV-FARE-00802 carries no ERP, toll, airport surcharge or other government-set or third-party pass-through line, so nothing is carved out of the full refund. The driver's argument that the trace alone cannot substantiate the deviation is rejected: POL-RD-07(ii) imposes an independent-corroboration requirement only when the trace is impaired, and this trace is not impaired.\n\nOther issues. EV-CHAT-00802 has zero messages, so POL-RD-04 cannot apply. EV-TRIP-00802 shows no endpoint amendment and vehicle_type RYDE_X, so POL-RD-05 and POL-RD-12 do not apply. EV-ADVIS-00802-01 is MISSING, weight 0.0, issue MISSING_ARTIFACT; no party relies on it as an external-cause exoneration, and its absence does not trigger POL-RD-10(5) here. No billing-integrity defect appears on EV-FARE-00802, so no POL-RD-09(4) referral is made. The identifiers match, no timestamps conflict, and no POL-RD-10 escalation trigger fires.\n\nConfidence and execution. The relied-on artifacts carry weight 1.0. The missing advisory carries 0.0 but does not carry the deciding fact. Confidence is 0.95, above the 0.70 floor. Because the monetary effect of SGD 19.65 exceeds the SGD 8.00 execution threshold, this provisional ruling is issued but the amount is held for human release under POL-GEN-05. The POL-RD-06(c) conduct referral does not delay or displace the refund."
  },
  "discarded_claims": []
}
